# FPS2 -- What load makes a fort slow? Ticks per wall second at the graphics cap 60, tick cap 1000, tool on, as each factor is scaled on BOATS (the user's 6x6 Boatsbowed copy, 29 citizens, 90 wild): wild land animals +200/+500 (cx-load wild, the tool's place), citizens +30/+60 (created dwarves made citizens by makeown, a working citizen's labors), caverns breached 1/3 (a stair shaft from the surface to each band's floor, the caves marked discovered), all three at once; and embark size 2x2/4x4/6x6 on fresh 7-dwarf embarks at CTRL's tile (region4 29,20). Throughput is the harness's ticks / wall seconds per 1,000-tick step, first step discarded.
